>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `CS_DEPTH_SOLVE_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.CS_DEPTH_SOLVE_TAC :
  {dup : bool} -> int -> clasetLib.claset -> NTactical.ntactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Constructs fixed-bound depth-first, solve-completely classical search.

`CS_DEPTH_SOLVE_TAC {dup} n cs` safely saturates a state, then searches the
first open goal using `cs`. Matching safe steps and unifying assumption,
contradiction, and zero-premise safe steps do not consume the bound.
Positive-premise instantiating and unsafe steps consume one unit on each
branch.

When `dup` is `false`, a unifying elimination or destruction rule is not
allowed to duplicate its major premise. When `dup` is `true`, duplicating
alternatives are available. A negative bound has no positive-resource
steps, although free steps can still solve a goal.

This raw interface takes a prepared claset, returns an `ntactic`, performs
no theorem-list processing, and does not make the result deterministic.

### Failure

Produces no result if no complete proof is found within the bound. If
kernel replay of an engine solution fails, search backtracks to another
solution; the tactic has no result if none can be replayed.

### Example

``` hol4
val depth_search =
  classicalLib.CS_DEPTH_SOLVE_TAC {dup = false} 4
    (clasetLib.the_claset ());
```

